 ## Step 0: housekeeping (before anything else)
 
-**Regression check (E-002 style), proposed by DR-007.** Rerun one Stage 3 arm-A seed on the current code: `python -m src.train --config configs/tuned/t1_base_two.yaml --seed 0` and compare its validation curve with the raw log of `final-t1-base-two` seed 0. Rule (fixed now): **PASS** if the validation accuracy at every evaluation step is identical on the same machine and library versions, or, on different hardware or versions, differs by at most 0.002 at every evaluation and gives the same steps-to-target. Otherwise stop and find the cause before any further run. Record the result as a verification entry.
+**Regression check (E-002 style), proposed by DR-007.** Rerun one Stage 3 arm-A seed on the current code with `python scripts/verify_regression.py` (it reruns `configs/tuned/t1_base_two.yaml` seed 0 under the stage name `verify-regression`, so the log cannot mix with the Stage 3 logs, and compares it with the raw log of `final-t1-base-two` seed 0; it also requires the logged FLOPs to be identical). Rule (fixed now, implemented in the script): **PASS** if the validation accuracy at every evaluation step is identical on the same machine and library versions, or, on different hardware or versions, differs by at most 0.002 at every evaluation and gives the same steps-to-target. Otherwise stop and find the cause before any further run. Record the result as a verification entry.
 
 Then record D-020 and update D-021 (the open items) so the choices below have an owner.
 
